title The ledger that could not book a red -- capacity was nobody's question
prompt The autonomous seat prompt: roster cold, reds first, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope; pick up the running thread.
think Rota N=3707, row 2 -- fire, the row that sees: what must stop, what must be cut. The card's Now block named "one structural" in a sentence whose numbers nobody had taken, so I took them.
think Measured: construction/REDS.md at 24,571 of the 24,576 its own header declares -- five bytes -- with all nine rows marked OPEN and a median row of 1,983, so reds_fold.sh refuses row_open on every one of them and rows_that_fit is zero. Four reds went unbooked on 20260828 for that reason; %335, %336 and %337 were born onto single-row shelves instead, and %337 is still live where the fold tool refuses to put a live row.
think Read the nine and the assumption under the fold rule comes apart: not one is open on an unrepaired defect -- two on ratchets, four on seats awaiting his word, three on booked laps -- and reds-first reserves booking for a red. The pin's single OPEN flag carries two meanings and the fold tool can only read the flag.
think Four meters read that page and every one was green, because each asks whether what is written is CONSISTENT and none asks whether anything more can be WRITTEN. That is REDS %301's sentence one instrument over, so the repair is a meter for the question nobody had asked.
obs The lap opened with the roster cold: 89 guards, 82 green, 7 red, tree_moved=no, all seven pre-existing since I had touched nothing. Closed the two mechanical ones on witnesses -- readme_metrics and geode_libraries, both regeneration drift, the "lap ended at git add" signature the card names. Five stand: rule_twin 39/36, ascii_comment 4,342/4,333, dated_path 335/168, and two Pond guards that are Hush's lane on a macOS bench.
obs Running my own scan on real data caught my own flaw: I had used the fold tool's loose bare-word test for BOTH questions, so it reported five live reds on shelves where one exists. Foldability and declared status are different questions; the row reader now answers each its own way, is spelled once and called twice, and the witness PROVES the count against reds_status_consistency_scan.sh rather than promising it -- pin=9 shelf=1 spine=10.
obs Two more reds inside the repair, both kept in the row rather than smoothed: the control's harness swallowed every expected refusal, since ( cmd ); echo $? under set -e aborts before the echo, so three cases read no while the scan was correct; and printf ate %1 as a conversion specifier, so the witness's deadlock case passed VACUOUSLY on zero rows before the green path beside it exposed both. That is REDS %311's lesson reproduced inside the lap citing it.
obs QA on touch: the essay first graded D+ 66 at register 60 -- 40% negative of 45 sentences, against Field's 30%. Rather than reclassify to meter and dodge the ceiling, I recast nine sentences to lead with what is, holding every figure and path exactly. Register 60 -> 80, and the three touched artifacts read A 91 / A 96 / A 96.
obs shelf_open_rows rose 1 -> 2 on this lap's own account, because %338 -- the red about a ledger with no room -- had no room to be written in. Raising a ceiling to admit your own row is worth saying out loud; the alternative was marking it closed while the deadlock stands.
obs The card is at 24,571 of 24,576 too, three bytes at the open, so its update was written to SHRINK rather than grow. Two living pins pressed against one bound is a second instance of the same shape, noted rather than widened into this lap.
